/-!
# Count-lattice contraction map for a five-party holographic facet (`facet6`)

This module isolates the single expensive definition here: the count-lattice
contraction map `facet6G`.  The 16 larger-side terms of the underlying holographic entropy
inequality fall into 10 *blocks* of equal regions (multiplicities `[3,3,1,1,3,1,1,1,1,1]`),
so the associated `{0,1}^16 -> {0,1}^18` contraction map factors through the 10 block
*popcounts*: `f = facet6G ∘ blockPopcounts`.  `facet6G` is a map on the finite count-lattice
`∏_b {0..coef_b}` (indexed here directly by the popcount tuple), and it is 1-Lipschitz on
lattice edges (adjacent popcounts differ by at most one output bit).  Keeping it in its own
module means its (large) elaboration is paid once and cached as `.olean`.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Facet6

/-- The block multiplicities `[3,3,1,1,3,1,1,1,1,1]` of the 10 distinct larger-side regions. -/
def coefs : Fin 10 → Nat := ![3, 3, 1, 1, 3, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]

/-- Starting input-bit index of each block within the 16 larger-side bits. -/
def blockStart : Fin 10 → Nat := ![0, 3, 6, 7, 8, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15]

/-- The 10 block popcounts of a 16-bit larger-side pattern `p`, as a `Fin 10 → Nat` vector.
Each block sums the `coefs b` consecutive input bits starting at `blockStart b`; a set bit
contributes `1`.  Written out explicitly per block so no bound proof is incurred. -/
def bit (p : Fin 16 → Bool) (i : Fin 16) : Nat := if p i then 1 else 0

def blockPopcounts (p : Fin 16 → Bool) : Fin 10 → Nat :=
  ![bit p 0 + bit p 1 + bit p 2, bit p 3 + bit p 4 + bit p 5, bit p 6, bit p 7, bit p 8 + bit p 9 + bit p 10, bit p 11, bit p 12, bit p 13, bit p 14, bit p 15]

/-- The count-lattice contraction map: a nested `match` on the 10 block popcounts
`n0 … n9` (each `nᵦ ∈ {0 .. coefs b}`), returning the 18-bit bounded-region pattern.
A lattice edge is a single `nᵦ ± 1`; this map is 1-Lipschitz on such edges. Kept in its own
module because this `match` is the single expensive elaboration here. -/
def facet6G : Nat → Nat → Nat → Nat → Nat → Nat → Nat → Nat → Nat → Nat → (Fin 18 → Bool)
